{"title":"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of these numbers is less than its reciprocal?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed2f4245f83690e22f8be391da28cbbe4b6c418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ {-2} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ {-1} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7748d3d38355a68b51bddc29d7647230728287e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227dc886bb89a6c016dc9a223ae91f5713b2e537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 &lt; -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/490e28cd3add569fd8172ada5406706827cbbeed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ {-2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" /> is correct.\n</p><p>The reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f1e85b935562e7bfe528d543f957192e5741b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, (B) is incorrect.\n</p><p>The reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is undefined, so (C) is incorrect.\n</p><p>The reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dec7050aa92389359debfb8b7fda5e4146d824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, (D) is incorrect.\n</p><p>The reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a373dd10cab795de8e6b2daeee2c49d23534f954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 &gt; \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, (E) is incorrect.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be a real number that is less than its reciprocal, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65d57c124fd8d861234b7d4b94e001bf705a31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a0901419c277658469226431138dfb5ede474b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> must be defined, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79c96e270e148516fb5dd4a73725d8be87c80c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f5227094edee764d64d78aaed6f61067ce5841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is negative, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458288efccddbfb352f59d2d2a3b78ff41c1670e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d269c9f239f1b12cce2c56a46feb219eca6247a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65d57c124fd8d861234b7d4b94e001bf705a31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" /> if and only if either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d269c9f239f1b12cce2c56a46feb219eca6247a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />.  Of the answer choices, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e05197cf4eedd343d8326c42e038eee0dfeb9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(A)}\\ {-2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" /> is a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Starting again with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65d57c124fd8d861234b7d4b94e001bf705a31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />, we avoid multiplication by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.   Instead, move everything to the left, and find a common denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65d57c124fd8d861234b7d4b94e001bf705a31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b771026940ffaa74b4b7f06b259f2e7f8073d81c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - \\frac{1}{x} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243011d40e74c0a6aead4d0a4d88dd77e32723b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2 - 1}{x} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a7b3bb8700b82752d362e1bc066d451fb0327b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+1)(x-1)}{x} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Divide this expression at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, as those are the three points where the expression on the left will \"change sign\".\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/35799beb782bb41ab8c36687823e108991d56136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, all three of those terms will be negative, and the inequality is true.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f498d2ffdafc7d28bbba71b26b37477a7fe0868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty, -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> is part of our solution set.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4698d50e185d539859a8538d97245d5fe6565a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 &lt; x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00ed6a7b53eca338b27229604a5e8706ca609ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> term will become positive, but the other two terms remain negative.  Thus, there are no solutions in this region.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, then both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00ed6a7b53eca338b27229604a5e8706ca609ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are positive, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> remains negative.  Thus, the entire region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is part of the solution set.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5de2084c7e917a3a832d007457243e240cf3929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then all three terms are positive, and there are no solutions.\n</p><p>At all three \"boundary points\", the function is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or undefined.  Therefore, the entire solution set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1677f6047341afcfd693f0c9a118d0bec27b4da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty, -1) \\cup (0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />, and the only option in that region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f226eebf91a88812cbbed46cd0a97e67530a7494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-2$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 8\">2000 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.p